    "items": [
      {
        "id": "def-locally-finite-homotopy-type",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Locally finite homotopy types and rational cardinality",
        "deps": [
          "def-homotopy-fiber-of-a-map"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "justified_by": [
          "lem-homotopy-fiber-component-weight-ratio"
        ],
        "statement": "A homotopy type $X$ is **locally finite** if every homotopy group $\\pi_i(X,x)$ is finite for every point $x$, and for each $x$ there is an integer $n_x$ such that $\\pi_i(X,x)=0$ for $i>n_x$.\n\nWrite $\\pi_0(X)$ for the set of connected components. Let $\\mathbb Q_c(X)$ be the rational-valued functions on $\\pi_0(X)$ with finite support. For a component $x$, the **homotopy weight** is\n$$\nw_X(x):=\\prod_{i>0}|\\pi_i(X,x)|^{(-1)^i}.\n$$\nThe product is finite because the positive homotopy groups vanish in high degrees; a negative exponent means a reciprocal.\n\nFor a map $f:X\\to Y$ of locally finite homotopy types and $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb Q_c(X)$, define\n$$\nf_!(\\alpha)(y):=\\sum_{x\\in\\pi_0(F_y)}\\alpha(i_y(x))\\,w_{F_y}(x),\n$$\nwhere $F_y$ is the homotopy fiber of $f$ at $y$ ([[def-homotopy-fiber-of-a-map]]) and $i_y:F_y\\to X$ is its natural map. For a proper map, meaning one whose homotopy fibers have finitely many connected components, also define $f^*:\\mathbb Q_c(Y)\\to\\mathbb Q_c(X)$ by $f^*\\beta=\\beta\\circ\\pi_0(f)$.\n\nThe ratio lemma [[lem-homotopy-fiber-component-weight-ratio]] proves that fibers of maps between locally finite homotopy types are locally finite and that the displayed sum is finite. The set of components of a homotopy fiber alone does not determine $f_!$."
      },
